--- crates/iwe/README.md
64: ### `find`
65: Search and discover documents.
66: 
67: ```bash
68: iwe find                           # list all documents
69: iwe find "search query"            # fuzzy match on title and key
70: iwe find --roots                   # only root documents (no incoming refs)
71: iwe find --refs-to project         # documents referencing "project"
72: iwe find --refs-from project       # documents referenced by "project"
73: iwe find -l 10                     # limit results
74: iwe find -f json                   # output as JSON
75: ```
76: 
77: Options:
78: - `--roots` - only root documents (no incoming block refs)
79: - `--refs-to <KEY>` - documents that reference this key
80: - `--refs-from <KEY>` - documents referenced by this key
81: - `-l, --limit <N>` - maximum results
82: - `-f, --format <FORMAT>` - output format: `markdown` (default), `keys`, `json`
83: 
84: ### `retrieve`
85: Retrieve document content with configurable expansion.
86: 
--- crates/iwe/help/find/long_about.txt
1: Search and discover documents in your knowledge base.
2: 
3: Uses fuzzy matching on document title and key. Without a query, documents are
4: sorted by popularity (incoming references count). Supports filtering by root
5: documents, reference relationships, and structural sub-document membership
6: via the --in / --in-any / --not-in / --max-depth selector.
--- crates/iwe/help/find/after_help.txt
1: OUTPUT FORMATS:
2: 
3: MARKDOWN (default, -f markdown):
4:   ## Documents
5: 
6:   Found 3 results:
7: 
8:   - [Document A](doc-a) (root)
9:   - [Document B](doc-b) <- [Document A](doc-a)
10: 
11:   Each result shows:
12:   - Document link
13:   - (root) indicator if no parents
14:   - Parent documents with <- notation (where this doc is embedded)
15: 
16: KEYS (-f keys):
17:   One key per line, suitable for piping:
18: 
19:     doc-a
20:     doc-b
21:     doc-c
22: 
23: JSON (-f json):
24:   Structured output with metadata:
25: 
26:     {"query": "...", "total": 3, "results": [
27:       {"key": "...", "title": "...", "is_root": true,
28:        "incoming_refs": 5, "outgoing_refs": 2, "parent_documents": [...]}]}
29: 
30: STRUCTURAL SET SELECTOR (--in family):
31: 
32:   --in KEY[:DEPTH]      Sub-documents of EVERY listed key (AND). Repeatable.
33:                         KEY:DEPTH overrides --max-depth per entry.
34:   --in-any KEY[:DEPTH]  Sub-documents of AT LEAST ONE listed key (OR).
35:   --not-in KEY[:DEPTH]  Exclude sub-documents of any listed key (NOT).
36:   --max-depth N         Default depth for entries without :DEPTH. Unbounded if omitted.
37: 
38: EXAMPLES:
39: 
40:   # Sub-documents of A AND B (intersection, unbounded)
41:   iwe find --in projects/alpha --in people/dmytro
42: 
43:   # Per-parent depth: A within 3 hops, Dmytro within 1
44:   iwe find --in projects/alpha:3 --in people/dmytro:1
