Fixed.

## Diagnosis

The bug was in bare-frontmatter wrapping, not in `find --meta`.

`find --meta depends=foo` parses stored metadata with `serde_yaml` and already handles YAML sequences correctly. Fenced front matter worked because the YAML reached the metadata parser intact.

Bare front matter goes through `wrap_bare_frontmatter()` in `crates/liwe/src/markdown.rs`, which synthetically wraps the leading bare metadata block in `---` fences so `pulldown-cmark` recognizes it as metadata. That wrapper was cleaning the header by dropping all lines that start with a space:

```rust
.filter(|l| !l.starts_with(' '))
```

So bare YAML like:

```yaml
title: Task A
depends:
  - foo
```

was turned into:

```yaml
title: Task A
depends:
```

before metadata filtering ran. Result: `depends` parsed as empty/null rather than as a sequence containing `foo`.

All tests passed because existing metadata-sequence tests only covered fenced YAML, and existing bare-frontmatter tests only covered flat scalar fields.

## Fix

Changed `wrap_bare_frontmatter()` to preserve indentation and only trim trailing whitespace from the header:

```rust
let cleaned_header = header.trim_end();
```

Then use `cleaned_header` when adding synthetic fences.

Files changed:

- `crates/liwe/src/markdown.rs`
- `crates/liwe/tests/find_metadata_test.rs`

## Regression test added

Added `value_in_bare_yaml_sequence_matches`, covering:

```yaml
title: Task A
depends:
  - foo
  - bar
```

with:

```rust
metadata_filters: vec![("depends".to_string(), "foo".to_string())]
```

and asserting the document is found.

## Verification

Ran:

```bash
cargo test -p liwe value_in_bare_yaml_sequence_matches -- --nocapture
cargo test
```

Both passed.

